{
  "slug": "go-palindrome-cuts",
  "title": "Fewest palindrome cuts",
  "kind": "code",
  "language": "go",
  "level": 4,
  "statement": "Cut a string into pieces so that every piece is a palindrome (reads the same forwards and backwards). Print the smallest number of cuts needed. A string that is already a palindrome needs 0 cuts.\n\nInput: one line holding a string s of lowercase letters (1 <= length of s <= 5000).\n\nOutput: one line with the minimum number of cuts. An O(n^3) solution is too slow for the largest tests; aim for O(n^2).\n\nExample\nInput:\nabaccd\nOutput:\n2\n(aba | cc | d)",
  "starter_code": "package main\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n\treader := bufio.NewReader(os.Stdin)\n\tvar s string\n\tfmt.Fscan(reader, &s)\n\t// Print the fewest cuts so that every piece is a palindrome\n\tfmt.Println(len(s))\n}\n",
  "time_limit_ms": 1000,
  "memory_limit_mb": 256,
  "comparator": "trim",
  "timer_seconds": 1500,
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "Example",
      "input": "abaccd\n",
      "expected_output": "2\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "Already a palindrome",
      "input": "racecar\n",
      "expected_output": "0\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "One letter",
      "input": "z\n",
      "expected_output": "0\n",
      "hidden": true
    },
    {
      "name": "All distinct",
      "input": "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\n",
      "expected_output": "25\n",
      "hidden": true
    },
    {
      "name": "One b in the middle",
      "input": "\n",
      "expected_output": "1\n",
      "hidden": true
    },
    {
      "name": "5000 sparse b",
      "input": "\n",
      "expected_output": "7\n",
      "hidden": true
    }
  ]
}
